      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CONNER'S RAIN (1) has shown good improvement at his last two starts, finishing in the money last time when 2nd at this track over 342m. Good beginner assisted by the inside draw. Makes plenty of appeal. SEBON DISCO (8) turned spotting a big start finishing fifth (23.75) last time in a Grade 6 at Mt Gambier. Solid record at the distance winning three races. The form out of the last run is proven to be strong. One of the better chances. VICTA WALLY (4) overcame a check to score a Grade 6 win at Murray Bridge over 455m latest, winning by one length (25.58). Does go very well at this course. Speedy runner who can find the front with a clear break off the middle. Expected to feature again. BOUNDING HOME (2) is worth a look despite no experience at this circuit.",
